## OPTIONAL - For Additional Features

```
# Advanced logging (Datadog, LogDNA, Sentry)
# DATADOG_API_KEY=your-key
# SENTRY_DSN=your-dsn

# File uploads to S3-compatible storage
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-key
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_BUCKET_NAME=your-bucket

# Or use Vercel Blob Storage
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_...

# Persistent sessions with Redis
# REDIS_URL=redis://default:password@host:6379

# Email service (SendGrid, Mailgun, etc.)
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.sendgrid.net
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=apikey
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your-api-key
```

---

## How to Add to Render

1. Go to [render.com/dashboard](https://render.com/dashboard)
2. Click your service: `rodb-news-platform`
3. Click **Environment** (or **Settings** → **Environment Variables**)
4. Click **Add Environment Variable**
5. For each variable:
   - **Key**: Copy from list above
   - **Value**: Copy corresponding value
   - Check **Add for all environments** (Production, Preview, Development)
   - Click **Add**
6. Once all added, service auto-redeploys
7. Check **Logs** to verify successful startup

---

## Values Reference

| Variable | Value | Notes |
|----------|-------|-------|
| NODE_ENV | `production` | Always this value |
| PORT | `10000` | Render default - don't change |
| LOG_LEVEL | `info` | Options: error, warn, info, debug |
| TURSO_CONNECTION_URL | `libsql://rodb-ganeshpoudel.aws-ap-northeast-1.turso.io` | Your database URL |
| TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN | `eyJhb...` | Your database token (full value) |
| JWT_SECRET | 64-char hex | Already generated, use as-is |
| JWT_REFRESH_SECRET | 64-char hex | Already generated, use as-is |
| SESSION_SECRET | 64-char hex | Already generated, use as-is |
| ADMIN_SECRET | 64-char hex | Already generated, use as-is |
| CRON_SECRET | 64-char hex | Already generated, use as-is |
| CORS_ORIGIN | `https://yourdomain.com` | Change to your frontend domain |
| FRONTEND_URL | `https://yourdomain.com` | Same as CORS_ORIGIN usually |

---

✅ Once all variables are added and service redeploys successfully, you're ready for production!
